layout: layouts/staff.njk
staffPage: settings
staffNum: "07"
staffTitle: Settings
staffHeading: How this <b>works</b>
staffHint: some of these change what the public sees
---
{#- Tabs rather than one long page: these groups have different audiences and
   different blast radii. Account affects only you. Languages and Keys change
   what a public website serves. Keeping them apart makes that difference
   visible before you touch anything, instead of after. -#}
<div class="tabs" role="tablist">
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="account" aria-selected="true">Account</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="languages" aria-selected="false">Languages</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="keys" aria-selected="false">API keys</button>
</div>

<span class="hint" id="setStatus"></span>

<!-- ------------------------------------------------------------ account -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="account" role="tabpanel">
  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3>Signed in as</h3>
      <p id="setEmail">—</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      {#- Access owns the identity, so there is no password here to change and
         pretending otherwise would send people looking for a control that does
         not exist. -#}
      <p class="note-inline">Your sign-in is managed by Cloudflare Access.
        Changing your email address or password is done there, not here.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3>Your access</h3>
      <p>What this account is allowed to do. Changed by an administrator, not
         here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <div class="role-tags" id="setRoles"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- The working-language control used to be here as well as on Languages,
     and the two were not kept in sync — the same setting in two places is one
     of them being wrong. It lives on Languages, next to the other language
     decisions. -#}
  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3>Your working language</h3>
      <p>Which language the milestone editor opens in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <p class="note-inline">Set this on the
        <button type="button" class="link-btn" data-goto="languages">Languages</button>
        tab, alongside the languages this site publishes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ---------------------------------------------------------- languages -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="languages" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  <p class="note">
    <b>These change what partner websites serve.</b> A language switched on here
    is offered to visitors; one switched off disappears from the public API.
    Translations you have already written are kept either way.
  </p>

  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3>Your working language</h3>
      <p><b>Affects only you.</b> Which language the milestone editor opens in.
         It changes nothing a visitor sees.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <select id="setPrefLang" class="lang-pick"></select>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3>Default language</h3>
      <p>What a visitor sees before choosing, and what a partner site falls back
         to when something has not been translated.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <select id="setDefaultLang" class="lang-pick"></select>
      <p class="note-inline" id="setDefaultNote" hidden>
        Only an administrator can change this.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-row set-row-block">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3>Published languages</h3>
      <p>Switch a language on to translate into it and serve it. The default
         language cannot be switched off.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control" id="setLangList"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- --------------------------------------------------------------- keys -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="keys" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  <p class="note">
    An API key lets a partner website read your <b>published</b> milestones and
    goal totals at build time. It can read nothing else — no contacts, no
    interactions, no drafts.
  </p>

  <div class="ms-bar key-create">
    <input type="text" id="setKeyName" class="key-name" maxlength="80"
           placeholder="What is this key for? e.g. chaseroush.com build">
    <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="setKeyAdd">Create key</button>
  </div>

  {#- Shown once, on creation, and never again — the database stores only a
     hash. Deliberately loud, because there is no second chance to copy it. -#}
  <div class="key-reveal" id="setKeyReveal" hidden>
    <h4>Copy this now — it cannot be shown again</h4>
    <code id="setKeyValue"></code>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="setKeyCopy">Copy</button>
    <p>Store it in the partner site's build environment as
       <code>THAUMA_API_KEY</code>. Never in a repository, and never in
       client-side JavaScript.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-list" id="setKeyList"></div>
</section>
